From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:05:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] AROS: volume and assign paths are absolute, also in file
 URLs

Problem: std counts only a leading / as a root on AROS, so a path such as
"RAM Disk:hx/pl.txt" (what the current directory is there) counted as
relative and the current directory was prepended again on every
canonicalisation; the status line showed it three times and saving
failed. url::Url::from_file_path refuses such paths, so saving panicked
in Document::identifier.
Change: helix_stdx::path::is_absolute treats a first component with a
colon as absolute on AROS; canonicalize, get_relative_path, symlink
targets, path completion and LSP file paths use it. helix_core::uri's
file_url and file_path_from_url map "Work:x" to file:///Work:x and back.
Repository: helix-editor/helix
Base: a05c151bb6e8e9c65ec390b0ae2afe7a5efd619b (tag 25.07.1)
Author: tomaszstaniak
Date: 2026-10-19
Platform scope: target_os = "aros" (x86_64 ABIv11); other targets unchanged.
Upstream status: local-only (not submitted).
Verification: on AROS One 1.3, opening pl.txt relative to RAM:hx shows
"pl.txt", and saving works there and in the root of RAM:.
